From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Johnson <105193579+Johnson-Anthony@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:20:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] HID: spi-hid: recover when a reset cuts off GET_FEATURE

A reset response is taken as the answer to whatever request is pending.
For GET_FEATURE that turned a device-initiated reset into a zero-filled
success: spi_hid_device_reset() never ran, so the reset was not counted,
the descriptors were not re-read and iptsd never re-applied its mode:
the stuck-in-default-mode case that the SL7 kit's patch 0008 exists for.
GET_FEATURE does not ask for a reset, so run the same recovery there.
SET_FEATURE keeps treating a reset as its answer, since a mode change
may reset the device.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/hid/spi-hid/spi-hid-core.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/spi-hid/spi-hid-core.c b/drivers/hid/spi-hid/spi-hid-core.c
index 0761a3111..ae3f19aab 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/spi-hid/spi-hid-core.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/spi-hid/spi-hid-core.c
@@ -388,7 +388,10 @@ static bool spi_hid_recent(unsigned long stamp, unsigned int ms)
 	return stamp && time_before(jiffies, stamp + msecs_to_jiffies(ms));
 }
 
-/* IRQ thread: the device sent a reset response that no request asked for. */
+/*
+ * The device sent a reset response that no request asked for: from the IRQ
+ * thread, or from a GET_FEATURE that got the reset instead of its answer.
+ */
 static void spi_hid_device_reset(struct spi_hid *shid)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &shid->spi->dev;
@@ -974,6 +977,11 @@ static int spi_hid_ll_raw_request(struct hid_device *hid,
 		}
 
 		if (shid->resp_type == SPI_HID_REPORT_TYPE_RESET_RESP) {
+			/*
+			 * GET_FEATURE does not ask for a reset, so the device
+			 * reset on its own and took this request's slot.
+			 */
+			spi_hid_device_reset(shid);
 			memset(buf, 0, len);
 			buf[0] = reportnum;
 			ret = len;
